</div>

<div class="sg-card">
<h3>About SecretGuard</h3>
<p><strong>What SecretGuard protects</strong></p>
<p class="sg-note">Unraid Docker templates are stored on the USB flash device. Credentials entered directly as Docker environment variables may therefore be stored in plaintext XML. SecretGuard detects likely credentials and lets you move selected values to dedicated protected storage while keeping the Docker configuration usable.</p>
<p><strong>Security boundary</strong></p>
<p class="sg-note">SecretGuard is not a replacement for host security. A user with root access to an unlocked server may be able to access Docker environment variables, mounted secret files or runtime credentials. Disk encryption and Vault primarily protect SecretGuard-managed credentials while their underlying storage is at rest.</p>
</div>
<script>
(function(){
  const buttons=[...document.querySelectorAll('.sg-tab-button')];
  const panels=[...document.querySelectorAll('.sg-tab-panel')];
  if(!buttons.length||!panels.length) return;
  function activate(name){
    if(!panels.some(p=>p.dataset.sgPanel===name)) name='overview';
    buttons.forEach(b=>{const on=b.dataset.sgTab===name;b.classList.toggle('sg-active',on);b.setAttribute('aria-selected',on?'true':'false');});
    panels.forEach(p=>p.classList.toggle('sg-active',p.dataset.sgPanel===name));
    try{localStorage.setItem('secretguard.activeTab',name);}catch(e){}
  }
  buttons.forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>activate(b.dataset.sgTab)));
  let saved='overview';
  try{saved=localStorage.getItem('secretguard.activeTab')||'overview';}catch(e){}
  activate(saved);
})();
</script>

